# Neo Learn Wavetable parameters (docs/specs/neo-learn.md, neo-learn-controls.md A1 and A2.4). The order is permanent: songs and
# presets store values by position. The 12 controls are the six core ones, then the six global ones (Attack, Decay, Sustain, Release,
# Unison / Spread, Output). Each has a snake_case id, and the Explain text (How, Sound; the description is the How line).
# Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoLearnWavetable
namespace NeoBuzz.LearnWt
class NeoLearnWavetableMachine
tracks 16
summary Teaching wavetable synth: one Dye Essence patch driven by 12 controls. A table (ten built in, or your own WAV) read at a position that an LFO can sweep, with Bend on the left of centre and hard Sync on the right of the phase warp (at High quality), a sine sub, an ADSR, unison and an output gain. Every control says what it does and what you will hear. Use it for evolving pads, sync leads, vocal and digital textures, or to learn how wavetable synthesis works.
import wavetable .wav | A WAV wavetable: frames of 2048 samples (or a clm chunk saying the frame size), or one short single cycle. It becomes the machine's "User" table (item 0), and Wavetable is set to User.

group Core
WtPosition       "Frame Pos" 0 1000 500 pct
    id wt_position
    how Selects and interpolates the active single-cycle waveform across the frames of the loaded table.
    sound Sweeps smoothly through changing timbral shapes, from dark fundamentals to complex harmonic structures.
PhaseWarp        "Phase Warp" 0 1000 500 bip
    id phase_warp
    how Bends the phase read within each cycle: left of centre pinches it (Bend), right of centre hard-syncs it (Sync).
    sound Pinches the waveform for nasal hard-sync tones or hollow pulse-width effects regardless of the selected table.
TableSelect      "Wavetable" 0 10 0 enum Basic PWM Harmonics Formants Sync_sweep FM_sweep Organ Resonant Digital Grit User
    id table_select
    how Selects one of Dye Essence's tables (Basic, PWM, Harmonics, Formants, Sync sweep, FM sweep, Organ, Resonant, Digital, Grit) or User, a table you load.
    sound Changes the fundamental sonic palette and harmonic progression of the oscillator.
ScanSpeed        "Motion Rate" 0 1000 500 freq 0.05 15
    id scan_speed
    how Sets the speed of the internal LFO/envelope generator that automatically moves the frame position.
    sound Controls whether the timbre evolves slowly like a cinematic pad or wobbles rapidly like a modulated bass.
ScanDepth        "Motion Depth" 0 1000 500 bip
    id scan_depth
    how Sets the travel distance and direction of the automatic wavetable frame scanner.
    sound At 0% the wavetable frame remains static; higher values animate the waveform across the table automatically.
SubAnchor        "Sub Anchor" 0 1000 0 pct
    id sub_anchor
    how Blends in a clean, unwarped fundamental sine wave at the root pitch.
    sound Keeps the low end solid and musical even when the main wavetable is heavily warped or bright.

group Global
EnvAttack        "Attack" 0 1000 250 time 0.0005 5
    id env_attack
    how Sets the time required for the note's amplitude (and routed envelope modulation) to ramp from silence to full peak after a note-on trigger.
    sound Low values create immediate, percussive plucks; high values produce slow, swelling pads.
EnvDecay         "Decay" 0 1000 594 time 0.005 8
    id env_decay
    how Controls how long it takes for the signal to drop from peak level down to the sustain level while a key remains held.
    sound Short decay makes notes snappy and tight; longer decay gives a gradual piano- or bell-like fade.
EnvSustain       "Sustain" 0 1000 700 pct
    id env_sustain
    how Defines the steady-state volume level maintained for as long as a note is held after the Attack and Decay stages complete.
    sound At 0% the synth behaves like a plucked or struck instrument; at 100% it holds full organ-like volume.
EnvRelease       "Release" 0 1000 515 time 0.005 10
    id env_release
    how Sets the time required for the sound to fade from its current level to complete silence after the note is released.
    sound Short release stops notes abruptly; long release leaves an ambient tail that blends chords together.
UnisonDetune     "Unison / Spread" 0 1000 0 pct
    id unison_detune
    how 0% plays one voice per note; above 0% each note plays 5 detuned, stereo-spread voices (3 in Additive, Granular and Spectral), with detune (up to ±50 cents) and width growing with the value.
    sound Thickens thin waveforms into wide, chorus-like stereo leads and pads.
OutputGain       "Output" 0 1000 775 db -36 12
    id output_gain
    how Sets the level after synthesis. There is no limiter (NeoBuzz mixes in floating point); a clip light shows when the output passes 0 dBFS.
    sound Controls overall loudness; keep the clip light dark when the next machine expects levels at or below 0 dBFS.

# What the machine measures (NeoLearnWavetableMachine.Readings, machine_readings): the output after Output, in dBFS.
reading rms_db dB | The output's RMS over about half a second (-inf: silence)
reading peak_db dB | The output's peak, falling 20 dB a second (-inf: silence)
reading active_voices notes | Notes sounding now (unison voices belong to their note)
